 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Compactifiable morphism",
 "statement": "A separated finite-type\nmorphism $f:X\\to S$ is *compactifiable* if it admits a\nfactorization $f=rj$ with $j:X\\hookrightarrow\\overline X$ an open\nimmersion and $r:\\overline X\\to S$ proper; such a factorization is a\ncompactification of\n$f$. Every morphism occurring in this chapter is compactifiable:\nfor a separated finite-type morphism of finite-type schemes over a\nfield, a compactification exists by\n[thm-nagata-compactification].",
 "source": {
